s to shigaraki's awakened decay  these two battles had been taking place  simultaneously for much of the arc as  the heroes attempted to raid  both locations at the same time and stop  the villains in their tracks  however the heroes failed to stop  gigantomachia from leaving the mansion  and heading towards shigaraki  and jakku and as a result makia has been  destroying  everything in his tracks and tearing  through entire cities  leaving nothing but death and  destruction in his path  as makia has been making his way towards  jakku and carrying dabi toga and other  villains on his back  the heroes including endeavor aizawa  deku bakugo and others  have been busy fighting shigeraki who  now possesses  all for one and its many quirks we have  seen a bunch of incredible twists and  turns during this battle  and the last thing that we saw was deku  and the former one for all users  repelling shigaraki  and all for one's attempt to steal one  for all it was heavily implied that  chigaraki was in bad  shape and that he must take a break and  recuperate before continuing the fight  against deku  and the other heroes luckily for  shigaraki  makia has arrived in jakku and so the  heroes now have more than just shigaraki  to worry about  but also luckily for shigaraki deku  hesitated to finish him  off deku knows what shigaraki has done  and what he is capable of doing in the  future  and even though deku has seen shigaraki  kill or severely injure pro heroes and  even some of his close friends like  bakugou  deku still expresses the hope that  shigaraki will stop  moving and stop fighting so that deku  doesn't have to finish him off  so in essence deku hesitates to kill  shigaraki  even though he arguably had the  opportunity to do so after shigaraki was  repelled  from the vestige world the latest  installment of the story takes us away  from the main battle against shigaraki  and this really showcases the sheer  extent of destruction that this arc has  brought on japan's hero society  we can see that dozens of heroes are now  rushing to take on gigantomachia  even though the odds of the heroes  succeeding and stopping him appear to be  quite slim  especially after what we saw back at the  mansion where nearly an entire army of  heroes and hero students  failed to stop him machia is a giant  moving at 100 kilometers an hour and  tearing through entire buildings with  his massive claws  he has been destroying his way through  city after city  causing widespread damage and who knows  how many civilian casualties  many of the heroes blame themselves for  this they failed to stop machia back at  the mansion  their big plan to neutralize the  villains has clearly failed  and now they must do everything in their  power to save as many innocent lives as  possible  even at the cost of their own lives and  beyond the pro heroes who are at least  licensed and experienced crime fighters  this latest war arc has also put the  inexperienced hero students  in the line of fire hero students are  now regularly finding themselves on the  front lines  and this further demonstrates just how  severe this situation is  the pro-hero system is crumbling in the  face of this  unprecedented villain threat  inexperienced 16 year olds are putting  their lives in danger right alongside  some of the toughest pro heroes  something that would have been virtually  unthinkable under different  circumstances  once makia and the villains on his back  finally make it to jakku after leveling  entire sections of multiple cities along  the way  toga uses this opportunity to disguise  herself as a civilian  and she then lures ochako into a trap  as ochako's life now hangs in the  balance because she was taking such a  risk to help evacuate  innocent civilians i couldn't help but  think that this is yet another reminder  about how much the hero society has  changed during this one single arc  don't get me wrong i don't think that  ochako bakugo and other important  characters are going to die  although they may be seriously injured  as was the case with bakugo  but what is happening to bakugou ochako  and many other hero students on the  front lines  is indicative of how game-changing this  arc  really is under the established rules  and regulations of the hero society  16 year old students with little  experience would never be allowed to  risk their lives fighting  overpowered villains like machia and  shigaraki this is a job for fully  licensed and experienced pro heroes  and under normal circumstances they  would be the ones handling such massive  villain threats  but these are not ordinary circumstances  the hero society as we knew it is gone  the villain threat  is just too great and the old rules and  regulations have gone out the window  and as the hero society itself is  changing as a result of this arc  so are the people who live in this  society including  deku we can't forget how deku started  out  he was an idealistic kid who idolized  pro heroes  and especially almight he believed in  the hero society  and its ideals and the concept that he  had of what a pro hero was supposed to  be  was the wholesome saturday morning  cartoon type of hero  just like all might this hero is good  and pure  he always puts others before himself and  while he brings villains to justice  he would never do something as well as  actually killing them and to be fair  in the world of saturday morning  cartoons the villains themselves are  usually much  less dark the villains are not going  around killing people  they're usually just causing havoc or  hatching some crazy plot which is always  foiled  by the heroes but boku no hero is  not a saturday morning cartoon there are  a lot of wholesome elements in mha  but there are also many serious elements  people really die  in this series and this includes  villains like twice  and heroes like sir nidai the villains  of boku no hero are not the villains of  saturday morning cartoons they are far  more dangerous  and deadly and this current war arc is a  perfect example of that  remember how deku reacted to the death  of sir nidai  the death of sir and the fact that meteo  lost his quirk  affected deku so much that he seriously  considered giving one for all to medio  since he was unable to save sir deku  immediately started thinking that he  wasn't worthy  of having one for all after all and  these types of insecurities continue to  haunt  deku every time something tragic happens  because he genuinely wants to save  everyone and so when anything bad does  happen  deku feels guilty for not being able to  prevent it  this current arc has gone out of its way  to remind us that deku  always puts others before himself and  that he is willing to go to impossible  lengths  to save others he is even prepared to go  against  common sense and put his life in  imminent danger  if it means living up to his own ideal  of what it means to be a hero  and now let's think about what has  happened so far during this  current arc we know how deku reacted to  the death of one pro hero  sir nidai so how is he going to react  now that dozens of heroes and who knows  how many civilians  are dead we know that the number 6 bro  hero crust  is dead we saw him die but there are  many other heroes who certainly died in  the aftermath of shigaraki's destruction  they just died off-screen i think washu  might have been one of them but we're  not sure as of right now  on top of that it's pretty clear that  countless civilians were likely killed  and injured during makia's rampage  through multiple cities  and there were definitely some serious  hero casualties back at the villain  mansion  as well finally multiple people who are  close to deku have already been  seriously injured  during this arc including bakugou aizawa  and gran torino even if the heroes win  the battle of jakku in the end  how do you think deku will react to all  this death  and all this suffering right now he is  focused on the battle at hand  but once he has time to actually take in  what happened  how do you think he will cope with the  fact that he simply couldn't  save everyone deku's character is going  to  change after this arc and he will never  be the same innocent and idealistic boy  again earlier in the arc we saw that  hawks was willing to go  all the way and he was willing to kill  twice in order to prevent him from using  sad man's parade to potentially kill  many others hawks didn't want to do it  and he tried giving twice  a way out but when twice refused to  listen  hawks did what he had to do and he  finished  the job he killed a villain to prevent  that villain from hurting others  in the future but unlike hawks deku  still  isn't the type of person who is prepared  to go all the way  he is not the type of person who is  prepared to kill  even if the targeting question is  shigaraki an incredibly overpowered  villain who has already killed dozens of  people deku just can't bring himself to  end shigaraki's life deku hesitates  hoping that shigaraki will just give up  and stop  fighting deku still wants to be the kind  of hero that you see  in saturday morning cartoons the hero  who brings villains to justice  and sends them to jail but not the hero  who gets his hands dirty by acting as  judge jury and executioner but imagine  what will  happen if after deku spares shigaraki's  life  shigaraki then goes on to kill more  people  maybe even someone close to deku how  will deku cope with the knowledge that  someone died because he  failed to act someone died because deku  refused to end  the threat posed by shigaraki once and  for all  this would absolutely break deku  and it would change him completely after  this arc  whether the heroes win or lose deku will  have to come  face to face with the tragic truth  you cannot be a saturday morning cartoon  hero  in a world that is much darker and much  more cruel  than the world of your average saturday  morning cartoon